learning/S122/evidence/red/browser-red-001--index.html.source:19: trailing whitespace.
+      <h2 id="constraints-heading">Hosting constraints, not native proof</h2>
learning/S122/evidence/red/browser-red-001--index.html.source:20: trailing whitespace.
+      <ul>
learning/S122/evidence/red/browser-red-001--index.html.source:21: trailing whitespace.
+        <li><strong>Linux code:</strong> choose a reviewed manual swap or an explicitly controlled
learning/S122/evidence/red/browser-red-001--index.html.source:22: trailing whitespace.
+          deployment/swap pipeline. Native auto-swap is unsupported.</li>
learning/S122/evidence/red/browser-red-001--index.html.source:23: trailing whitespace.
+        <li><strong>Windows code:</strong> auto-swap is documented for eligible code-slot configurations;
learning/S122/evidence/red/browser-red-001--index.html.source:24: trailing whitespace.
+          that does not confer support on Linux. Windows is not rehearsed here.</li>
learning/S122/evidence/red/browser-red-001--index.html.source:25: trailing whitespace.
+        <li><strong>Web App for Containers:</strong> native auto-swap is also unsupported; see source S123.</li>
learning/S122/evidence/red/browser-red-001--index.html.source:26: trailing whitespace.
+        <li>Deployment slots require a supported Standard, Premium or Isolated plan.
learning/S122/evidence/red/browser-red-001--index.html.source:27: trailing whitespace.
+          This fictional Standard example is not an approved native SKU, region or resource.</li>
learning/S122/evidence/red/browser-red-001--index.html.source:28: trailing whitespace.
+        <li>Two slots share the same <strong>two plan workers</strong>. Adding a slot, changing routing or
learning/S122/evidence/red/browser-red-001--index.html.source:29: trailing whitespace.
+          swapping content does not add compute, capacity isolation or a separate failure domain.</li>
learning/S122/evidence/red/browser-red-001--index.html.source:30: trailing whitespace.
+        <li>Production is the target. Review effective target settings, meaningful readiness,
learning/S122/evidence/red/browser-red-001--index.html.source:31: trailing whitespace.
+          compatible state and overlap headroom. Default swap warm-up accepts any HTTP response
learning/S122/evidence/red/browser-red-001--index.html.source:32: trailing whitespace.
+          unless acceptable statuses are specified; this fixture requires HTTP 200 plus all gates.</li>
learning/S122/evidence/red/browser-red-001--index.html.source:33: trailing whitespace.
+        <li>Native swaps recycle former production workers and can abandon long operations.
learning/S122/evidence/red/browser-red-001--index.html.source:34: trailing whitespace.
+          Keeping the old slot is not draining protection. Continuation below is fictional application data.</li>
learning/S122/evidence/red/browser-red-001--index.html.source:35: trailing whitespace.
+        <li>Zero-percent routing is not access control. Slot-bound settings do not follow content.
learning/S122/evidence/red/browser-red-001--index.html.source:36: trailing whitespace.
